# Corpus automations + LoRA FT (F75–F77)

Guardrails for EV-027. Specs: [Corpus: feature-list.md §F75–F77], ADR-052, ADR-053,
RD-325–348.

## F75 — Corpus change automations

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Enqueue **catch-up** only (failed/partial/missing embed; optional retag) | Re-embed when embeddings already complete |
| Triggers: job completion, cron catch-up, doc CRUD → **async** Modal job | Sync heavy work on the write-API request path |
| Idempotent key = `document_id` + `revision` | Blind duplicate enqueue without dedupe |
| **One** Modal schedule with F76; distinct `job_type`s | Separate sprawl crons without ADR |
| Kill-switch + concurrency/cost caps; DM enable/disable + Postgres run history | Auto **F41 rebuild** on every change; #192 dashboard widgets (out of scope) |

## F76 — Freshness

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| Default stale threshold **30 days** (`VECINITA_FRESHNESS_STALE_DAYS`) | Invent a different default without RD/ADR |
| Hash-aware refresh; bump `last_checked` even when unchanged | Fire F75 catch-up side effects from freshness beyond shared schedule infra |
| Per-source enable/disable + Refresh now | Guarantee third-party site uptime |

## F77 — LoRA fine-tune + human promote

| Do | Do not |
|----|--------|
| **LoRA/PEFT** on pinned Qwen; instruction/QA **SFT** pairs from chunks | Full-weight FT as default |
| **Manual operator approve** before each GPU train | Auto-start train on schedule without approve |
| Present base vs adapter **eval evidence**; promote = **human judgment only** | Automated numeric abort / auto-promote on metric |
| Load adapter on prod **`vecinita-llm` only after promote** | Auto-load latest adapter on prod |
| Playground may load candidates pre-promote | Blind promote without operator review |
| AskQuestion before **live prod** FT cutover | Promote FT to live prod unprompted |
| Rollback = clear promoted pin → base | Leave orphan adapters as silent prod default |

FT train/serve is **not** antibody `src/finetune/` (F8 template). Use
`infra/modal/finetune_app.py` (`vecinita-llm-finetune` + volume `llm-finetune-adapters`)
+ `llm_app.py` per ADR-053 / TP4.

## Shared

- Respect `VECINITA_AUTOMATIONS_KILL_SWITCH` for F75 enqueue and F77 train start.
- FT caps: `VECINITA_FINETUNE_MAX_CONCURRENT` (default 1),
  `VECINITA_FINETUNE_MAX_RUNS_PER_DAY` (default 3) — TP5 / RD-348.
- Prod corpus mutation via automation/freshness still requires AskQuestion —
  see [no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc](no-live-prod-corpus-push.mdc).

